in @optics/source/ganglion

# @optics/source/ganglion/fate — gain medium for the fate ganglion
# (the selector / final tournament arbiter).
#
# Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §10.1, Fate's `fate` ganglion
# (also named `fate-the-selector` in §10 prose; canonical substrate
# name `fate` per `boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror`'s `type ganglion =
# abyss | introject | cartographer | explorer | fate`) performs final
# tournament selection via `@ai/fate.select(hole)` (per
# `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror`). At the optical altitude, fate is
# the 5th and terminal 90-port diffractive surface in the 5-layer
# D²NN (per §10.3, Lin et al. 2018); its output couples to the
# detector that resolves the tournament verdict (per §10.1, the
# brightest detector port wins).
#
# The source declaration here carries the active gain that drives
# fate's transit during the kintsugi loop's ACTIVE pass (per §10.2).
# At the cavity-resonator altitude, fate's gain medium IS the load-
# bearing one for the ACTIVE pass's resolution: §10.2 identifies the
# kintsugi loop's `is_settled(authentic)` verdict with the laser
# threshold condition (gain * pump >= loss); fate's gain medium is
# the one whose pumping crosses threshold to emit the tournament
# verdict.
#
# === Energy-balance declarations (per spec §3.9) ===
#
#   action       — `refract`. Per §10.3, phase-only diffractive transit.
#   formalism    — `s_matrix`. 90×90 multi-port topology.
#   energy       — `active`.
#   pumping      — `io(channel: ref)`. Per recognition #57.
#   gain_curve   — `ref` at @meta/ast. Per §4.9, substrate-pull leaves
#                    physical measurement to @io. v2 candidate: fate's
#                    gain curve specializes to a single sharp eigenmode
#                    around the consonant-basis fixed point (per
#                    `shards/epistemologic/math/music/dissonance.mirror`'s
#                    Helmholtz/Plomp-Levelt grounding) — the cavity
#                    lases on its ground-mode λ_0 (per §10.2).
#   sat          — `ref` at @meta/ast. v2 candidate: fate's saturation
#                    envelope corresponds to the consent surface's
#                    pass/partial/failure verdict thresholds (per
#                    `shards/kintsugi/consent.mirror`).
#
# === Why uniform with the other 4 ganglia at v1 ===
#
# Per `shards/optics/source/ganglion.mirror` header: v1 lands all 5
# ganglion sources with uniform shape; fate's specialization (the
# sharpest peak; the lowest threshold; the cavity-ground-mode
# anchor) is documented above for v2 but NOT encoded in this tick's
# carrier shape — substrate-pull-realize lands the spec-faithful
# first declaration; per-ganglion specialization requires a parametric
# gain-curve type that does not yet exist in `shards/glass.mirror`
# (STOP-condition 4 territory, surfaced not triggered: the per-
# ganglion gain profiles differ ENOUGH that v1 uniform is honest,
# and v2 needs parametric carrier types). The v2 substrate-pull lands
# when the energy-balance opacity map surfaces the differentiation
# at runtime.
#
# === Recognition #58 Surface B closure ===
#
# Fifth and final of 5 sources closing recognition #58's v1 gap (per
# Seam's adversarial review verdict). Together with abyss, introject,
# cartographer, and explorer, this tick discharges the
# `source_declares_energy_balance` property's requirement for the
# kintsugi loop's `oscillate.gain` to exist as active sources in the
# active-spectrometer bench (per §12.3, Brown 2003 cavity-enhanced
# reading).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.7, §3.9, §10.1
#               (fate IS selector ganglion), §10.2 (laser threshold
#               identification), §10.3 (D²NN identification), §10.8
#               (Surface B).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]].
# Related shards: boot/std/fate.mirror (the family root; declares
#                 `type model = abyss | introject | cartographer |
#                 explorer | fate`),
#                 boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror (`fate` variant),
#                 boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror
#                 (`@ai/fate.select(hole)`),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the resonator whose
#                 ACTIVE pass this source drives to the laser
#                 threshold; the load-bearing identification),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the detector that reads
#                 fate's output; the pass/partial/failure thresholds
#                 are saturation envelopes).

source @optics/source/ganglion/fate {
  action:     refract,
  formalism:  s_matrix,
  energy:     active,
  pumping:    io(channel: ref),
  gain_curve: ref,
  sat:        ref,
  in:         aperture(@optics/aperture/splinter),
  out:        aperture(@optics/aperture/connectome),
}

out @optics/source/ganglion/fate
